- ArrayList is Dynamic Array that allow to store multiple objects of any class. but there are no fix size.
It Was added to the java programing in JDK 1.2 as part of the java collection framework.

- Present in java.util.package.
- ArrayList is Resizable array tha can be Shrink in the memory whenever needed.
- java ArrayList using DynamicArray Internally for storing group of elements, objects or Data.
- Arraylist class also implements 3 markar interface serializable,Cloneable and RandomAccess.
- In that all Markat interface doesnot any method or any member of variable. if is also colled empty interface because
no feied or no methods present.

- FETURES OF ARRAYLIST:
  - Resizable Array: Arraylist is a Resizable or growable that means Size of array list is increase or decrease.
  - Index Besed Structure :
  - Insertion Order: It maintain the Insertion order.
  - Null element: Array list store null element.
  - Non -syncronize: It is non syncronize it means multiple thread use in same time in array list.
  - Duplicate element: Duplicat element stores in Arraylist.

- Performance: performance is low because Any element remove in array list Shifting of all elements.

